        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293">

                <pb facs="0644" n="620" xml:id="pg620"/>

                <head>293. Memorandum From the President’s Military Representative’s Naval Aide
                    (Bagley) to the President’s Military Representative (Taylor)<anchor n="0"
                        xml:id="d293-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-02-12">February 12,
                        1962</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Attached notes outline situation in Laos as of today.</p>
                <p>The contingency paper<anchor n="1" xml:id="d293-f2"/> you have already seen is
                    pertinent, but does not direct itself to the new approach to Souvanna. This
                    raises new questions as to the role of the King which I have cited.</p>
                <p>Our tactics are pretty well set. I suggest the need now is to discuss the
                    contingencies in detail, and that should be the emphasis with the
                        President.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d293-f3"/> State has had a tendency to
                    discuss pros and cons of short-term procedures without facing future
                    consequences.</p>
                <p>I checked with DOD(ISA) on their views on our Laos policy. Their main point is to
                    repeat Ambassador Brown’s warning that when we go direct to Souvanna, we burn
                    all bridges with Phoumi/Boun Oum, probably regardless of the outcome.</p>
                <p>Sec/State and his advisors will have a full-blown talk on SEATO tomorrow.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d293-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">WHB</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d293-a1.xml" xpointer="d293-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d293-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d293-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Defense University, Taylor Papers, Laos 7, T–028–69. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d293-f2" n="1" xml:id="d293-f2-content">
                <p>The President met with Harriman, Taylor, and McGeorge Bundy at the White House
                    from 4:15 to 6:20 p.m. The meeting was characterized as “off the record” and no
                    other account of it has been found. (Kennedy Library, President’s Appointment
                    Book)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d293-f3" n="2" xml:id="d293-f3-content">
                <p>Apparent reference to a State/Defense paper summarized in <ref target="#d292"
                        >Document 292</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d293-f4" n="3" xml:id="d293-f4-content">
                <p>An account of that meeting is included in <ref target="frus1961-63v23">volume
                        XXIII</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
